# Git commits

Only commit when the user explicitly asks.

## Message style (match history)

Short, plain English, imperative or factual — like existing history:

- `fixed multiflex ptt issue`
- `Add .vscode and .git to .gitignore`
- `Update README.md`
- `final 1.1.0`

Prefer one line. Mention version or breaking config changes when relevant. No Conventional Commits required (`feat:`, `fix:` optional, not mandatory).

## Do not

- Commit secrets, local Flex IPs if the user wants privacy, or `node_modules`
- Amend/push unless the user asks
- Empty commits
